---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';

// Written against the UK GDPR Article 13 checklist and the ICO's "right to be
// informed" guidance. Everything here describes what the site and the business
// actually do today — see the note in the cookie policy about the one embed
// that is not first-party. When the enquiry forms are wired to a real endpoint
// (SITE-BACKLOG.md § 6, they currently discard input), the "How we collect it"
// and "Who we share it with" sections need the form handler adding.
---

<LegalPage
  title="UK Vehicle Exporters Privacy Notice"
  description="How UK Vehicle Exporters Ltd collects, uses and protects your personal data when you enquire about or book a vehicle export, and the rights you have over it."
  heading="UK Vehicle Exporters Privacy Notice"
  crumb="Privacy Notice"
  updated="4 September 2026"
>
  <div class="note">
    <p>
      This notice explains what we do with your personal information when you contact us about exporting a
      vehicle, when we ship one for you, and when you use this website. It is written to meet our obligations
      under the UK GDPR and the Data Protection Act 2018.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    UK Vehicle Exporters Ltd is the <strong>data controller</strong> for the personal data described in this
    notice. That means we decide why and how it is used.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Registered in England and Wales, company number <strong>10399100</strong></li>
    <li>Registered office: Penstraze Business Park, Chacewater, Penstraze, Truro, England, TR4 8PN</li>
    <li>Email: <a href="mailto:sales@vehicleexports.co.uk">sales@vehicleexports.co.uk</a></li>
    <li>Telephone: <a href="tel:+441872491409">+44 (0)1872 491409</a></li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We have not appointed a Data Protection Officer, because we are not required to. Any question about this
    notice or about your data should go to the address above, marked for the attention of the data protection
    contact.
  </p>

  <h2>What personal data we collect</h2>
  <p>What we hold depends on how far you get with us.</p>

  <h3>If you make an enquiry</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Your name, email address and telephone number</li>
    <li>The country and port you want the vehicle shipped to</li>
    <li>Details of the vehicle you want us to source, buy, ship or export</li>
    <li>Anything else you choose to tell us in the message</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>If we go on to source, buy or ship a vehicle for you</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Your full name and both your UK and destination addresses</li>
    <li>
      Identity documents where the export, customs or anti-money-laundering rules require them — typically a
      passport or photographic ID, and proof of address
    </li>
    <li>
      Vehicle documents: V5C registration details, VIN, purchase invoice, and the export and customs paperwork
      raised against them
    </li>
    <li>Payment details and a record of the payments made. We do not store full card numbers</li>
    <li>Our correspondence with you, including emails, WhatsApp messages and notes of telephone calls</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>If you visit this website</h3>
  <p>
    Our hosting provider records standard server log information, including the IP address the request came
    from, the pages requested, and the date and time. This is ordinary technical logging used to keep the site
    running and secure. We do not run analytics, advertising or tracking software on this site. See our{' '}
    <a href="/cookie-policy">Cookie Policy</a> for what is stored on your device and what third-party content
    the site loads.
  </p>

  <h2>How we collect it</h2>
  <p>
    Almost always directly from you — by telephone, email, WhatsApp, through a form on this site, or in person.
    Where you ask us to buy a vehicle on your behalf, we may also receive information about you from the seller
    or dealer involved in that purchase, and where we arrange shipping we receive booking confirmations from
    the carrier that contain your details.
  </p>

  <h2>Why we use it, and our lawful basis</h2>
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>What we use it for</th><th>Lawful basis</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Answering your enquiry and preparing a quotation</td>
          <td>Steps taken at your request before entering a contract</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Sourcing, buying, inspecting, collecting and exporting a vehicle for you</td>
          <td>Performance of our contract with you</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Booking the sailing and raising the Bill of Lading and export documents</td>
          <td>Performance of our contract with you</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>UK customs export declarations and DVLA notification</td>
          <td>Compliance with a legal obligation</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Keeping accounting, VAT and export records</td>
          <td>Compliance with a legal obligation</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Identity and anti-money-laundering checks where they apply</td>
          <td>Compliance with a legal obligation</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Keeping our own records of a job, and defending or bringing a legal claim</td>
          <td>Our legitimate interests in running and protecting the business</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Sending you our email newsletter, if you sign up for it</td>
          <td>Your consent, which you can withdraw at any time</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    We do not sell your personal data, and we do not use it for automated decision-making or profiling.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>
    Exporting a vehicle is not something we can do alone, and the people below need your details to do their
    part of it. We share only what each of them needs.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Shipping lines and ferry operators</strong> — to book the sailing and issue the Bill of Lading</li>
    <li><strong>Port agents, terminals and freight forwarders</strong> at the load port and the destination port</li>
    <li><strong>HM Revenue &amp; Customs and the DVLA</strong> — export declarations and notification of permanent export</li>
    <li><strong>Customs authorities and clearing agents in the destination country</strong>, where you ask us to introduce you to one</li>
    <li><strong>Transport and inspection contractors</strong> who collect, move or inspect the vehicle in the UK</li>
    <li><strong>Couriers</strong> — UPS and DHL, who carry the original export documents to you</li>
    <li><strong>Our bank, accountants and professional advisers</strong></li>
    <li><strong>Our IT and hosting suppliers</strong>, who process data on our instructions only</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We will also disclose information where the law requires it, or where it is necessary to establish, exercise
    or defend a legal claim.
  </p>

  <h2>Sending your data outside the UK</h2>
  <p>
    Exporting a vehicle means sending information to the country the vehicle is going to. To land a car in, for
    example, Kenya or Jamaica, the carrier, the destination port agent and that country's customs authority all
    need the consignee's name and address. Many of those countries have no UK adequacy decision.
  </p>
  <p>
    Where the transfer is necessary to perform the contract you have asked us to enter into, or to conclude a
    contract in your interest, we rely on that necessity as the basis for the transfer. Where we transfer data
    to a supplier for our own purposes rather than to complete your shipment, we put an International Data
    Transfer Agreement or the UK Addendum to the EU standard contractual clauses in place. You can ask us which
    applies to your shipment.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Enquiries that do not become a booking:</strong> up to 2 years from your last contact with us, so
      we can pick up the conversation if you come back to us.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Completed exports:</strong> at least 6 years from the end of the relevant tax year, because HMRC
      requires us to keep VAT, customs and accounting records for that long. Export documents may be kept
      longer where a shipment could still be the subject of a claim.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Identity and anti-money-laundering records:</strong> 5 years from the end of the business
      relationship, as the regulations require.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Newsletter sign-ups:</strong> until you unsubscribe.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Keeping it secure</h2>
  <p>
    We take appropriate technical and organisational measures to protect your data, including restricting access
    to the people who need it, using reputable suppliers, and serving this website over an encrypted connection.
    No transfer over the internet can be guaranteed completely secure, so please do not send us identity or
    payment documents by unencrypted email unless you are content to do so.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under the UK GDPR you have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Be told what we hold about you, and get a copy of it</li>
    <li>Have inaccurate data corrected</li>
    <li>Have data erased, where we have no continuing reason to keep it</li>
    <li>Restrict how we use it while a question about it is resolved</li>
    <li>Object to processing we carry out on the basis of our legitimate interests</li>
    <li>Receive data you gave us in a portable format, where we hold it by consent or under a contract</li>
    <li>Withdraw consent at any time, where consent is what we relied on</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Some of these rights are qualified — we cannot, for instance, delete a customs record we are legally
    required to keep. To exercise any of them, contact us at{' '}
    <a href="mailto:sales@vehicleexports.co.uk">sales@vehicleexports.co.uk</a>. We will respond within one
    month.
  </p>

  <h2>Complaints</h2>
  <p>
    If you are unhappy with how we have handled your data, please tell us first so we can put it right. You also
    have the right to complain to the Information Commissioner's Office, the UK supervisory authority, at{' '}
    <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint</a>
    or on 0303 123 1113.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this notice</h2>
  <p>
    We update this notice when what we do with personal data changes. The date at the top shows when it was last
    revised. Where a change is significant, we will say so on this page.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
